*******************************************************************************
* cap_cmomf - ngspice wrapper around the Verilog-A (OSDI) compact model
*             (ihp-sg13cmos5l metal fringe MoM capacitor, Metal1..Metal4)
*
* Copyright 2026 IHP PDK Authors
* Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License").
*
*******************************************************************************
* *** FITTED TO EM SIMULATION -- NOT VALIDATED ON SILICON ***
* Density and dead rim are fitted to Palace results on drawn geometry.
* Treat the result as an engineering estimate.  What each number rests on is in
* libs.tech/verilog-a/cap_cmomf/README.md.
*******************************************************************************
*
* Metal fringe (finger) capacitor on the cmos5l thin-metal stack: every metal
* layer from mmin to mmax carries a comb of fingers whose orientation
* alternates from layer to layer.  It is the fringe-style sibling of cap_cmomi,
* not a replacement for it: the two have different geometry and densities.
*
*   C = dens(mmin, mmax) * (l - 2 rim) * (w - 2 rim)
*     Metal1..4  1.107 fF/um^2, rim 0.207 um
*     Metal2..4  0.852 fF/um^2, rim 0.193 um
*     Metal3..4  0.504 fF/um^2, rim 0.121 um
*     others     estimates, see the Verilog-A
*
* rfmodel=0 (default) is the capacitance and its temperature coefficient only.
* rfmodel=1 adds series R and L, dielectric loss and a substrate branch on each
* plate, at a run-time cost, so set it where the loss matters.  subscale scales
* the plate to substrate capacitance, about 0.57 inside an array.  Do not add
* hand-made series or substrate elements around a device with rfmodel=1.
*
* The subckt stays 2-terminal: the Verilog-A SUB terminal is tied to node 0 here,
* as for cap_cmomi.
*
* Requires the OSDI object to be loaded first (done in libs.tech/ngspice/.spiceinit):
*   osdi $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/cap_cmomf.osdi
* Build it with libs.tech/verilog-a/openvaf-compile-va.sh.
* Simulator scope: ngspice via OSDI (built with -D__NGSPICE__), gnucap through
* capacitor_paramset.va.  Xyce and qucs-s are not wired.
*
* w,l in metres; mmin/mmax metal indices (1=Metal1 .. 4=Metal4).
* m: parallel device multiplier (ngspice subckt multiplier).
*******************************************************************************
* STATISTICAL / CORNER MODELING:
* cornerCAP.lib overrides the parameters below after including this file.  They
* are estimates from the line-width, thickness and sheet resistance limits of
* the process specification, not measured spreads.  C and R move in opposite
* directions, because narrow, thin metal lowers C and raises R.
*   cmomf_cscale  factor on C
*   cmomf_rscale  factor on the metal series R
*   cmomf_mm      1 enables local mismatch, gated per instance by mm_ok
*******************************************************************************

.param cmomf_cscale=1 cmomf_rscale=1 cmomf_mm=0

.subckt cap_cmomf PLUS MINUS w=5e-6 l=5e-6 mmin=1 mmax=4 subblock=0 mm_ok=1 rfmodel=0 subscale=1
.param m=1
.param mmz={mm_ok*cmomf_mm*agauss(0,1,1)}
Ncap PLUS MINUS 0 cap_cmomf_mod w={w} l={l} mmin={mmin} mmax={mmax} subblock={subblock} rfmodel={rfmodel}
+ subscale={subscale} cscale={cmomf_cscale} rscale={cmomf_rscale} mmz={mmz} m={m}
.model cap_cmomf_mod cap_cmomf
.ends cap_cmomf
